    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22116": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University | DFA Instructor, 1.0 FTE Limited Term Contract (1 Year)",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | DFA Instructor, 1.0 FTE Limited Term Contract (1 Year) Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants DFA Instructor, 1.0 FTE Limited Term Contract (1 Year) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title DFA Instructor, 1.0 FTE Limited Term Contract (1 Year) Posting Number F794P Type of position Limited Term Department/Unit Occupational Therapy Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada About the opportunity The School of Occupational Therapy in Dalhousie’s Faculty of Health invites applications from qualified candidates for a 12-month full-time limited-term faculty position at the Instructor rank (subject to final budgetary approval). This academic position encompasses teaching, teaching support, lab coordination, fieldwork teaching, and fieldwork support in the MSc(OT) entry-to-practice program. This position reports to the Dean of the Faculty of Health through the Director of the School of Occupational Therapy. There is no expectation of a research workload associated with this position. The position is available to begin immediately following the completion of the search process, or at a mutually agreed-upon date. Dalhousie University is comprised of 6,000 faculty and staff among its 13 faculties. Current enrollment is 21,000+ graduate and undergraduate students across four campuses. As part of Canada’s U15 research-intensive group, Dalhousie University is an influential driver of the region’s intellectual, social, and economic development. It is the largest university in Atlantic Canada and is located on the ancestral and unceded territory of the Mi’kmaq in the heart of Halifax (Kjipuktuk). This scenic coastal city is the capital of Nova Scotia. Nova Scotia is home to 13 Mi’kmaq First Nations, a deeply rooted African Nova Scotia community, and an increasingly diverse population which also includes a vibrant workforce of people living with (dis)Abilities. The Faculty of Health’s faculty, staff, and students are committed to improving the well-being of individuals, families, communities, and populations through diverse health programming, collaborative research, and strong community partnerships. The Faculty of Health is one of the largest faculties at Dalhousie, comprised of eight schools, one college, and one program, over 1,000 employees, and more than 3,000 students. With the most programmatically diverse health faculty in Canada, offering 45 academic programs, diplomas, and certificates at the entry, graduate, and advanced professional levels, our students are exposed to a broad range of health topics and learning experiences. Known for its theory-driven approach, commitment to social justice, and diverse educational approaches, the School of Occupational Therapy’s vision is advancing well-being in everyday life through occupation, leadership, community, and challenging the status quo. Key responsibilities of the position include developing and delivering course content, instructing and evaluating students across the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy program. The role also supports the Fieldwork Program and related initiatives, contributes to interprofessional health education, and assists with lab coordination, tutor training, and teaching support activities such as student evaluations and simulated client exams. Additional duties may include contributing to administrative functions within the School of Occupational Therapy and the Faculty of Health. Candidates must hold an entry-level degree in Occupational Therapy (a Master’s degree is preferred) and be licensed with the Nova Scotia Occupational Therapy Regulator ( NSOTR ), with at least three years of clinical experience, one year of teaching-related experience, and experience conducting and supporting research projects. They should demonstrate strong knowledge of current competencies, equity-focused and anti-oppressive teaching practices, the ability to support fieldwork education and preceptor development, and the ability to teach research courses and supervise MScOT student research projects. Excellent communication, organization, leadership, and time management skills are essential, along with a commitment to professional development. Preferred qualifications include proficiency with online platforms such as Brightspace, demonstrated ability in course development, lab coordination, simulation, and student evaluation methods such as OSCEs. Applications must include a cover letter stating qualifications and experience; a Curriculum Vitae; a statement of teaching experience and interests; copies of teaching evaluations (if available); and a copy of license with the NSOTR (upload as “Portfolio”). For further information regarding this position, contact: Dr. Paula Rushton, Director School of Occupational Therapy Faculty of Health prushton@dal.ca This position is a part of the Dalhousie Faculty Association ( DFA ) Bargaining Unit. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/11/2026 Close Date 09/08/2026 Open Until Filled No Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/21491 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover Letter Teaching Statement Portfolio List of referees Optional Documents Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
