    "https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22080": {
      "title": "Dalhousie University | Program Development Coordinator (Internal Posting)",
      "description": "Dalhousie University | Program Development Coordinator (Internal Posting) Skip to Main Content JOBS AT DALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About Dalhousie The Dalhousie Impact Working at Dal Equity, Diversity and Inclusion Talent Pathways Student Employment Hiring a Student FAQS for applicants Program Development Coordinator (Internal Posting) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Program Development Coordinator (Internal Posting) Research Project Department/Unit Work-Integrated Learning & Co-operative Education (WIL Co-op) Location Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada Posting Number S272-26 Employee Group DPMG Position Type Term Duration of Contract (if applicable) 2 years Employment Type Full Time Full-time Equivalency (FTE) 1.0 Salary $63,337 – $84,730 per annum, 35 hours per week Classification ADM-05 Provisional Statement This is a provisional classification. Formal regular review classification procedures may be initiated at any time by the incumbent or supervisor after the incumbent has worked a minimum of six months in the role. About Dalhousie University Dalhousie University is Atlantic Canada’s leading research-intensive university and a driver of the region’s intellectual, social and economic development. Located in the heart of Halifax, Nova Scotia, with an Agricultural Campus in Truro/Bible Hill, Dalhousie is a truly national and international university, with more than half of our almost 21,000 students coming from outside of the province. Our 6,000 faculty and staff foster a vibrant, purpose-driven community, that celebrated 200 years of academic excellence in 2018. Job Summary The Work‑Integrated Learning & Co‑operative Education office at Dalhousie University is responsible for securing and managing high-quality work term opportunities for almost 2,000 students annually in 27 Co-op and Work-Integrated Learning ( WIL ) programs across several faculties. Reporting to the Director, the Program Development Coordinator will design, develop, implement, assess, and enhance comprehensive curricular, co-curricular and professional development programming for students enrolled in Work-Integrated Learning programs delivered by Work-Integrated Learning & Co-operative Education ( WIL Co-op) in collaboration with supported faculties. Key Responsibilities Lead the design, development, implementation, and evaluation of innovative work-integrated learning ( WIL ) and co-operative education programs that support strategic priorities and evolving stakeholder needs. Develop and deliver curriculum, professional development programming, and learning resources that prepare students for workplace success, career development, and lifelong learning. Monitor emerging trends, best practices, and quality standards in WIL and experiential education to continuously enhance programs, student learning outcomes, and stakeholder engagement. Conduct program assessment, evaluation, environmental scans, and quality assurance activities to ensure curricula and programming remain effective, competitive, and aligned with national standards and accreditation requirements. Collaborate with faculty, students, employers, community partners, and university departments to develop, improve, and align WIL programs, curriculum requirements, and educational objectives. Provide leadership, expertise, and support for institutional projects, initiatives, committees, and partnerships that advance work-integrated learning and experiential education across the university. Note Applications for this position are restricted to current employees of Dalhousie University as described in the Internal Posting Guidelines . The successful applicant will be eligible for hybrid work (combination of in-person work on campus and remote work from within Nova Scotia) as agreed by all parties based on operational requirements and university guidelines. Required Qualifications Undergraduate degree in related discipline with three to five years of experience working in a a comparable client-based setting (or an equivalent combination of training and experience). Strong interpersonal and communication (verbal and written) skills. Strong time management and prioritization skills with the proven ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Self-motivated with the proven ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Proficiency in MS Office and the demonstrated ability to learn new programs. Assets Certificate or Degree in Adult Education, Career Education, Counselling or Career Coaching. Direct experience working within a university environment especially in Work-Integrated Learning. Job Competencies The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate proficiency in Dalhousie’s core and leadership competencies (https://www.dal.ca/dept/leaders.html), in particular: - Respect & Inclusion - Adaptability - Knowledge & Thinking Skills - Communication - Service Additional Information Dalhousie University supports a healthy and balanced lifestyle. Our total compensation package includes a defined benefit pension plan, health and dental plans, a health spending account, an employee and family assistance program and a tuition assistance program. Application Consideration Applications for this position are restricted to current employees of Dalhousie University as described in the Internal Posting Guidelines . We sincerely appreciate all applications and note that only candidates selected for an interview will be contacted directly by the hiring department or People and Culture. Diversity Statement Dalhousie University commits to achieving inclusive excellence through continually championing equity, diversity, inclusion, and accessibility. The university encourages applications from Indigenous Peoples of Turtle Island (especially Mi’kmaq), persons of Black/African descent (especially African Nova Scotians), and members of other racialized groups, persons with disabilities, women, persons identifying as members of 2SLGBTQIA+ communities, and all candidates who would contribute to the diversity of our community. In accordance with our Employment Equity Policy, preference will be given in hiring processes to candidates who self-identify as members of one or more of the equity-deserving groups listed above. For more information, including details related to our Employment Equity Policy and Plan and definitions of equity-deserving groups please review our Employment Equity information. If you require any support for the purpose of accommodation, such as technical aids or alternative arrangements, please let us know of these needs and how we can be of assistance. Dalhousie University is committed to ensuring all candidates have full, fair, and equitable participation in the hiring process. Our complete Accommodation Policy can be viewed here . Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Open Date 08/24/2026 Close Date 09/11/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://dal.peopleadmin.ca/postings/22024 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Résumé / Curriculum Vitae (CV) Optional Documents Cover Letter Dalhousie University Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada  B3H 4R2 1-902-494-2211 Agricultural Campus Truro, Nova Scotia, Canada  B2N 5E3 1-902-893-6600 Contact Us | Campus Directory | Campus Maps Media Centre | Privacy Statement Terms of Use To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
